//! # Zamani Native AST — Pattern
//!
//! Production-ready, source-level representation and common contract for
//! Zamani pattern nodes.
//!
//! ## Architectural position
//!
//! ```text
//! Zamani source
//!     │
//!     ▼
//! lexer
//!     │
//!     ▼
//! parser
//!     │
//!     ▼
//! Native Pattern AST
//!     │
//!     ├── wildcard.rs
//!     ├── identifier.rs
//!     ├── literal.rs
//!     ├── tuple.rs
//!     ├── struct.rs
//!     ├── enum.rs
//!     ├── range.rs
//!     ├── or.rs
//!     └── reference.rs
//!     │
//!     ▼
//! structural validation
//!     │
//!     ▼
//! semantic analysis
//!     │
//!     ▼
//! semantic model
//!     │
//!     ▼
//! ZUIR
//!     │
//!     ├── classical IR
//!     ├── quantum IR
//!     ├── hybrid IR
//!     ├── distributed IR
//!     ├── accelerator IR
//!     └── future-domain IR
//!     │
//!     ▼
//! target lowering / execution
//! ```
//!
//! ## Responsibility
//!
//! This module owns the **common source-level contract for native Zamani
//! patterns**.
//!
//! It provides:
//!
//! - the canonical pattern-node identity contract;
//! - pattern classification;
//! - deterministic direct-child enumeration;
//! - local structural validation;
//! - configurable validation policy;
//! - stable schema identification;
//! - integration with the common [`Node`] / [`AstNode`] infrastructure;
//! - source-level pattern invariants;
//! - diagnostics-friendly classification.
//!
//! It does **not** own concrete pattern variants.
//!
//! Concrete patterns belong to sibling modules:
//!
//! - `wildcard.rs`;
//! - `identifier.rs`;
//! - `literal.rs`;
//! - `tuple.rs`;
//! - `struct.rs`;
//! - `enum.rs`;
//! - `range.rs`;
//! - `or.rs`;
//! - `reference.rs`.
//!
//! ## Important architectural distinction
//!
//! This module represents **syntax**, not semantic pattern meaning.
//!
//! It must never perform:
//!
//! - name resolution;
//! - type inference;
//! - type checking;
//! - exhaustiveness analysis;
//! - reachability analysis;
//! - binding analysis;
//! - ownership analysis;
//! - borrow checking;
//! - resource allocation;
//! - quantum mapping;
//! - quantum routing;
//! - scheduling;
//! - calibration;
//! - QEC;
//! - noise analysis;
//! - backend selection;
//! - hardware mapping;
//! - QIR lowering;
//! - LLVM lowering;
//! - MLIR lowering;
//! - runtime execution.
//!
//! Those responsibilities belong to later compiler layers.
//!
//! ## Domain neutrality
//!
//! Patterns are intentionally domain-neutral.
//!
//! A pattern may eventually match:
//!
//! - classical values;
//! - symbolic values;
//! - resource handles;
//! - quantum measurement results;
//! - generic resources;
//! - distributed values;
//! - accelerator values;
//! - extension-defined values;
//! - future computational values.
//!
//! None of those interpretations belongs in this file.
//!
//! For example, a pattern matching a quantum measurement result is still a
//! source-level pattern. Whether that result controls quantum execution is
//! determined by semantic analysis and later lowering.
//!
//! ## POCO-REAF
//!
//! This module contains no assumptions about:
//!
//! - machine size;
//! - CPU architecture;
//! - GPU architecture;
//! - FPGA architecture;
//! - QPU architecture;
//! - qubit count;
//! - register width;
//! - number of resources;
//! - number of machines;
//! - vendor;
//! - backend;
//! - topology;
//! - gate set;
//! - instruction set.
//!
//! Therefore a pattern can participate in a program intended to scale from a
//! tiny execution environment to an arbitrarily large environment supported by
//! later compilation and execution layers.
//!
//! ```text
//! Program Once
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! Source Pattern
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! Semantic Meaning
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! ZUIR
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! Available Resources
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! Target Realization
//! ```
//!
//! ## Repository integration
//!
//! The common AST infrastructure currently provides:
//!
//! - [`Node`];
//! - [`NodeId`];
//! - [`NodeKind`];
//! - [`CoreNodeKind`];
//! - [`NodeMetadata`];
//! - [`Span`];
//! - [`AstNode`].
//!
//! This module builds only on those foundational contracts.
//!
//! The repository's `NodeKind` architecture intentionally has a core and an
//! extensible extension form, allowing future language constructs without
//! coupling the native AST to a fixed computational technology. The pattern
//! abstraction follows that same design principle. 
//!
//! ## Dependency boundary
//!
//! Allowed dependencies:
//!
//! - `core`;
//! - standard-library collection/iterator primitives;
//! - `serde`;
//! - foundational AST node modules.
//!
//! Forbidden dependencies:
//!
//! - parser;
//! - lexer;
//! - semantic analysis;
//! - compiler driver;
//! - ZUIR;
//! - quantum IR;
//! - QEC;
//! - optimization;
//! - scheduling;
//! - routing;
//! - calibration;
//! - runtime;
//! - hardware;
//! - vendor APIs;
//! - QIR;
//! - LLVM;
//! - MLIR.
//!
//! ## Concrete-pattern integration
//!
//! Concrete sibling pattern modules should implement the [`PatternNode`] trait.
//!
//! Conceptually:
//!
//! ```text
//! PatternNode
//!      │
//!      ├── WildcardPattern
//!      ├── IdentifierPattern
//!      ├── LiteralPattern
//!      ├── TuplePattern
//!      ├── StructPattern
//!      ├── EnumPattern
//!      ├── RangePattern
//!      ├── OrPattern
//!      └── ReferencePattern
//! ```
//!
//! The exact concrete representation remains owned by those modules.
//!
//! This prevents this file from becoming a giant closed enum that must be
//! edited whenever a new source-level pattern form is introduced.
//!
//! ## Structural validation boundary
//!
//! Local validation can verify:
//!
//! - the node has a pattern-compatible node kind;
//! - the pattern has a valid identity;
//! - direct child references do not point to the pattern itself;
//! - caller-supplied child-count limits are respected.
//!
//! Local validation cannot verify:
//!
//! - whether child IDs exist;
//! - whether a referenced identifier exists;
//! - whether a literal has the expected type;
//! - whether bindings are unique;
//! - whether a range is semantically valid;
//! - whether a match is exhaustive;
//! - whether a pattern is reachable;
//! - whether a pattern is valid for a quantum/classical resource.
//!
//! Those require graph-wide validation or semantic analysis.
//!
//! ## Scalability
//!
//! There is no language-level maximum for:
//!
//! - pattern count;
//! - pattern depth;
//! - number of match arms;
//! - number of bindings;
//! - tuple width;
//! - list width;
//! - program size;
//! - machine size;
//! - quantum-resource count.
//!
//! Resource limits may be supplied explicitly by compiler infrastructure.
//!
//! Such limits are **resource/security policies**, not language semantics.
//!
//! ## Determinism
//!
//! Direct children are returned in source-structural order.
//!
//! No hash-map iteration order is used to define pattern semantics.
//!
//! Concrete patterns must preserve their source ordering.
//!
//! ## Serialization
//!
//! This module uses Serde-compatible types but does not define a separate
//! serialization protocol.
//!
//! Repository-wide AST serialization owns:
//!
//! - global schema versioning;
//! - format selection;
//! - compatibility policy;
//! - migration;
//! - persistence.
//!
//! ## Security
//!
//! This implementation:
//!
//! - contains no `unsafe`;
//! - performs no I/O;
//! - executes no user code;
//! - uses no raw pointers;
//! - uses no global mutable state;
//! - performs no unchecked indexing;
//! - performs no recursive traversal;
//! - does not dereference `NodeId`s.
//!
//! Untrusted references remain opaque until validated by the AST graph.
//!
//! ## Rust compatibility
//!
//! Required toolchain:
//!
//! - Rust 1.97;
//! - Rust 1.97.1;
//! - edition 2021;
//! - stable Rust;
//! - no nightly features;
//! - no `unsafe`.
//!
//! ## No-reedit contract
//!
//! This file should require modification only when the **common source-level
//! pattern contract** changes.
//!
//! Changes to:
//!
//! - quantum backends;
//! - QPU topology;
//! - QEC;
//! - routing;
//! - scheduling;
//! - calibration;
//! - optimization;
//! - ZUIR;
//! - hardware;
//! - runtime;
//! - vendor integrations
//!
//! must not require modification here.
//!
//! ============================================================================
//! Implementation
//! ============================================================================

